# My everyday loaf based on morph

starter:
  ap_flour
  water
  hydration = 100%

leaven:
  starter
  bread_flour = 5 * starter
  cold_water
  extra = -20g
  hydration = 100%

wet:
  cold_water
  old_dough = 100g
  flourless_starter = 10%
  ascorbic_acid_1p = 50ppm * 100 * grain
  leaven = 40%
  olive_oil = 5%
  honey = 5%
  yogurt = 5%

grain:
  prairie_gold
  hard_red
  barley = 5%
  spelt = 5%
  buckwheat = 5%

dry:
  grain
  vwg = 3%
  potato_flakes = 5%
  flaxseed_meal = 5%
  yeast = 0.5%
  salt = 1.8%

dough:
  wet
  dry
  hydration = 70%
  # old_dough = 0 - wet.old_dough # forgot to remove it
  # 200g/L of flour
  # total_flour = 660g # 13 inch
  total_flour = 500g # 9 inch
  # total = 1086g

/*
August 13, 2026

Changes
- Adding flaxseed meal
- Use old dough and take it out at the end

Starter is 6 days old.

I started about 7:40

Mixed the leaven about 21:50 left on the counter.

Leaven pH = 3.71 at 8:09 dt is 78F. It rose to the top of the 500ml
container and had started to fall.

Dry T=84. Wet T=62. 

Used the KA for mixing. Mixed about 8:20. Stopped after 2 minutes;
it cleaned the bowl. DT after mixing is 72F. RT is 78F. 

30 minute rest in fridge.

Kneaded 7 minutes in KA. It was cleaning the bowl and looking great.

Into the cambro and the fridge at 8:20. S&F every 30 minutes.

Into the pan at 13:40. Left on the counter at 77F.

Forgot to remove the old dough. Doh! 100g of dough into fridge.

Let it rise too long!

Baked at 16:25 for 45 minutes at 350F lid off.

I added 100ml of water to the pan before preheating the oven.

Looks good but too large by 100g.

*/

